<title>FRANCE: Sagem wins U.S. Omnipoint phone contract.</title>
<headline>Sagem wins U.S. Omnipoint phone contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French electronics company Sagem said on Friday it has won a contract to supply mobile telephones to U.S. operator Omnipoint Corp for a network in the New York area.</p>
<p>Sagem gave no details of the contract value in its statement. The telephones use the PCS telecommunications standard.</p>
<p>Omnipoint's operating licence covers more than 40 million potential consumers and makes it the fifth largest PCS operator in the United States, it said. Sagem has turnover of 15 billion francs. -- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
